    "updated_at": "2022-09-26T15:20:55Z",
    "body": "Starship is in the `$PATH` and unfortunately initialing it before the global bashrc didn't help. But after your answer I tried to init Starship with a very minimal bashrc and it worked. So, I started to disable my Bash config line by line and found the instruction which actually breaks Starship initialization.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nexport PROMPT_COMMAND=\"history -a\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have no idea why there was no problem before the update (I use Starhip for almost a year) or how it related to global bashrc.\r\n\r\nThank you very much for your help!",
